Subject: [PATCH] cmd: Keep ERRORLEVEL at 0 when DEL finds no file to delete.

On Windows, DEL sets ERRORLEVEL only for bad or missing parameters; deleting a file that
does not exist (or cannot be deleted) prints a message and leaves ERRORLEVEL at 0. Wine
set 1, so batch files ending with a clean-up DEL exited with 1 and installers treated
them as failed (Maxon App 2024: "err.sys.script-execution-failed: Script execution
failed for task: preflight", from `del /f "%PROGRAMDATA%\Maxon\Service\mx1trial.inf"`).

Applied to the Proton-CachyOS 11.0 build as a binary patch by lib/patch_runner.py.
---
--- a/programs/cmd/builtins.c	2026-10-02 14:58:42.302840811 +0300
+++ b/programs/cmd/builtins.c	2026-10-02 14:58:42.312725332 +0300
@@ -1568,10 +1568,9 @@
             continue;    /* skip options */
 
         argsProcessed = TRUE;
-        if (!WCMD_delete_one(thisArg))
-        {
-            errorlevel = ERROR_INVALID_FUNCTION;
-        }
+        /* Like Windows, files that are missing or cannot be deleted leave ERRORLEVEL at 0;
+         * only bad or missing parameters set it. */
+        WCMD_delete_one(thisArg);
     }
 
     /* Handle no valid args */
